WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.193 --> 00:00:03.458
When consciousness is lost, the cause can be hidden.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:08.990
Seizure, metabolic illness, or benzodiazepine intoxication can look alike.

3
00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:13.324
This study turned carefully selected, twenty-second EEG segments

4
00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:16.080
into maps of how brain signals connect.

5
00:00:16.397 --> 00:00:19.870
Nineteen EEG channels. Five frequency bands.

6
00:00:20.078 --> 00:00:24.998
An AI model learned patterns across three causes in one hundred fifty patients.

7
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.223
In cross-validation, the model reached eighty-eight percent accuracy,

8
00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:32.672
with an AUC of zero point nine zero five.

9
00:00:33.002 --> 00:00:37.112
Testing on thirty new patients correctly classified twenty-five.

10
00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:39.716
Slow brain rhythms carried important clues.

11
00:00:40.057 --> 00:00:42.014
These are promising research findings.

12
00:00:42.256 --> 00:00:44.942
Larger, diverse external studies are still needed.

13
00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.964
Decode the network. Understand the difference.

14
00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:49.514
Toward clearer answers.
